  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIVA Substantive and Equal participation for a legally binding Plastic Treaty</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is co-developed by NIVA, CIEL, CEJAD and EIA. It will ensure substantive and equal participation of government officials and civil society actors from developing countries and economies in transition throughout the negotiations for an international legally binding instrument to end plastic pollution. The geographical focus will be on three regions (the Pacific, Africa and Asia) and the proposed target groups are state delegates participating in the INC process and civil society actors (CSAs). Within these three regions, the project will target specific country champions - Rwanda, Senegal, Indonesia, Viet Nam, Samoa and the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM).</narrative>
  </description>
